'''''Euphorbia segetalis''''', the '''grainfield spurge''', is a species of annual herb in the family [[Euphorbiaceae]]. They have a self-supporting growth form and simple, broad leaves. Flowers are visited by ''[[Plagiolepis pygmaea]]'', ''Polistes'', and nomad bees. Individuals can grow to 16&nbsp;cm tall.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Euphorbia segetalis L. - Encyclopedia of Life|url=https://eol.org/pages/1143928|access-date=2022-02-04|website=eol.org}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|last=Mifsud|first=Stephen|date=2002-08-23|title=Euphorbia segetalis (Pine Spurge) : MaltaWildPlants.com - the online Flora of the Maltese Islands.|url=https://www.maltawildplants.com/EUPH/Euphorbia_segetalis.php|access-date=2022-02-16|website=www.maltawildplants.com|language=en-us|archive-date=2021-12-27|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211227194231/https://www.maltawildplants.com/EUPH/Euphorbia_segetalis.php|url-status=dead}}</ref>

